.TH SDL_GetGlobalMouseState 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetGlobalMouseState \- Query the platform for the asynchronous mouse button state and the desktop-relative platform-cursor position.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_mouse.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_MouseButtonFlags SDL_GetGlobalMouseState(float *x, float *y);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function immediately queries the platform for the most recent asynchronous state, more costly than retrieving SDL\(aqs cached state in
.BR SDL_GetMouseState ()\[char46]
.PP
Passing non-NULL pointers to
.BR x
or
.BR y
will write the destination with respective x or y coordinates relative to the desktop\[char46]
.PP
In Relative Mode, the platform-cursor\(aqs position usually contradicts the SDL-cursor\(aqs position as manually calculated from
.BR SDL_GetMouseState ()
and
.BR SDL_GetWindowPosition \[char46]
.PP
This function can be useful if you need to track the mouse outside of a specific window and
.BR SDL_CaptureMouse ()
doesn\(aqt fit your needs\[char46] For example, it could be useful if you need to track the mouse while dragging a window, where coordinates relative to a window might not be in sync at all times\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I x
a pointer to receive the platform-cursor\(aqs x-position from the desktop\(aqs top left corner, can be NULL if unused\[char46]
.TP
.I y
a pointer to receive the platform-cursor\(aqs y-position from the desktop\(aqs top left corner, can be NULL if unused\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a 32-bit bitmask of the button state that can be bitwise-compared against the
.BR SDL_BUTTON_MASK (X)
macro\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CaptureMouse (3),
.BR SDL_GetMouseState (3),
.BR SDL_GetGlobalMouseState (3)
